mehr@oskar.uchicago.edu (David Mehringer) writes:

>In article <LCL.92Feb28140940@splinter.coe.northeastern.edu> lcl@splinter.coe.northeastern.edu (Lisa C. Lewis) writes:
>>
>>When writing on blank scrolls with a magic marker, does one write, for example,
>>"identify" or, depending what the scroll is in that game, "TEMOV"?  Or does it
>>matter?  Also, should the blank scroll be blessed or the marker be blessed - 
>>or again, can it work either way?
>>
>One must write "identify", "remove curse", etc.  You have to have read a
>scroll of that type before you can write it.  To get a blessed scroll, the
>blank scroll should be blessed.

It is true that you can bless a blank scroll and use an uncursed marker to get
a blessed scroll, but blessing each scroll is a very inefficient way to do it.
If you bless the marker, it improves the cursed/uncursed/blessed status of the
scroll as you write (ie: uncursed scroll + blessed marker = blessed scroll). The
only disadvantage to blessing your marker is you cannot write cursed scrolls of
genocide with a blessed marker, while you can with an unblessed one.

Also, you must have previously identified the scroll you wish to write.
For example, you can't write a blessed scroll of charging to recharge your
marker until you have already found and identified a scroll of charging
(use the \ command to check what scrolls you have identified).

